_G = {
 "Auto-Hacker": "When you make an ability check to pick a lock, hack a locked piece of Magical Technology, or disarm a trap, you can treat a d20 roll of 9 or lower as a 10.",
 "EMP": "Requires level 11. You can cast Electromagical Pulse without a spell slot or Material components. When you cast it this way, Magical Technology you wear or carry is not affected. Once you use this Gadget, you cannot use it again until you finish a Short Rest or Long Rest.",
 "Flux Cannon": "A blaster-like device with a row of lenses that shifts the temperature of matter. When you take the Attack action, you can replace one attack with firing it at a Large or smaller creature or object, or a 5-foot Cube, that you can see within 30 feet. Choose Freeze or Heat. **Freeze.** A creature makes a Constitution save, taking 2d8 Cold damage on a failure or half on a success. Materials react as well: most liquids freeze at once and metals turn brittle and shrink a little. **Heat.** A creature makes a Constitution save, taking 2d8 Fire damage on a failure or half on a success. Most liquids boil at once and metals glow red-hot and turn malleable. **Gadget Upgrade.** The damage rises by 1d8 at Gadgeteer levels 11 (3d8) and 17 (4d8).",
 "Magic Item": "You gain one magic item of your choice from the Magic Item Gadgets table, as long as you meet its Gadgeteer level. If it needs Attunement, it does not count against your attunement limit. If it calls for a saving throw, it uses your Gadget save DC. Items listed with a number in parentheses are consumable, and that number is how many you have. You regain all consumed items when you finish a Long Rest. **Repeatable.** You can take this Gadget more than once, each time with a different item. **Level 2 options.** Attractor Mine (3), Blaster Mod (Beam Module), Blaster Mod (+1 Enchanted Battery), Blaster Mod (Extended Barrel), Blaster Mod (Ricochet Barrel), Blaster Mod (Scope), Blaster Mod (Thermal Sights), Bottled Lightning (3), Deck of Holding (Expanded Storage), Dome Projector (1), Flashbang (1), Gravity Nullifier (3), Holo-Companion, Invisibomb (1), Motion Tracker, Shield Emitter, Spider Pod (3), Universal Translator, Weapon Wheel. **Level 5 options.** Blaster Mod (Aimbot), Blaster Mod (Electrocoil), Diode Beam, Flamethrower, Gravity Gun, Hoverboard, Jetpack, Scout Scanner. **Level 11 options.** Blaster Mod (+2 Enchanted Battery), Drive Wheel, Shoulder Cannon. **Level 17 options.** Blaster Mod (+3 Enchanted Battery), Death Ray, Skeleton Keycard.",
 "Magnet Boots": "While you wear these boots, you can move up, down, and across vertical surfaces and along ceilings with your hands free. You have a Climb Speed equal to your Speed. In a Zero-Gravity environment, you can also pull yourself to any surface within 100 feet as if it had normal gravity.",
 "Micro-Missiles": "When you take the Attack action, you can replace one attack with a barrage of micro-missiles. Each creature you choose in a 10-foot Emanation from you makes a Dexterity save, taking 2d4 Force damage on a failure or half on a success. **Gadget Upgrade.** The damage rises by 1d4 at Gadgeteer levels 11 (3d4) and 17 (4d4).",
 "Omni-Grenade": "Requires level 5. When you take the Attack action, you can replace one attack with throwing this explosive up to 30 feet. It detonates in a 10-foot-radius Sphere. Choose Fire, Ice, or Lightning. Each creature in the Sphere makes a Dexterity save. Once you use this Gadget, you can build a replacement when you finish a Short Rest or Long Rest. **Fire.** 4d8 Fire damage on a failure, half on a success. Each time you roll an 8 on one of these d8s, you can roll another d8 and add it, repeating on further 8s. You can add at most a number of extra dice equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum 1). **Ice.** 4d8 Cold damage and the creature's Speed is halved until the start of your next turn. A success means half damage and no Speed loss. **Lightning.** 4d8 Lightning damage and the creature cannot make Opportunity Attacks until the start of its next turn. A success means half damage only. **Gadget Upgrade.** The damage rises by 1d8 at Gadgeteer levels 11 (5d8) and 17 (6d8).",
 "Psionic Ray": "This Gadget fires a blast of psionic energy. When you take the Attack action, you can replace one attack with aiming it at a creature you can see within 120 feet. The target makes a Wisdom save, taking 2d6 Psychic damage on a failure or half on a success. **Gadget Upgrade.** The damage rises by 1d6 at Gadgeteer levels 11 (3d6) and 17 (4d6).",
 "Rocket Fists": "You have rocket-powered robotic gauntlets that mirror your gestures. When you take the Attack action, you can replace one attack with launching them, choosing Remote Control or Rocket Punch. They return to you at the end of your turn. **Remote Control.** The gauntlets fly up to 30 feet from you to handle an object, open an unlocked door or container, stow or fetch an item in an open container, or pour out a vial. They cannot attack except with Rocket Punch, cannot activate magic items or Gadgets, and each carries at most 25 pounds. **Rocket Punch.** A creature you can see within 30 feet makes a Dexterity save, taking 2d6 Bludgeoning damage on a failure or half on a success. **Gadget Upgrade.** The damage rises by 1d6 at Gadgeteer levels 11 (3d6) and 17 (4d6).",
 "Sentry Turret": "Requires level 5. As a Utilize action, you deploy this folding device in an unoccupied space you can see within 10 feet, where it becomes a Small, stationary blaster turret. Recovering it is also a Utilize action. The turret has AC 15, Hit Points equal to three times your Gadgeteer level, and Immunity to Poison and Psychic damage. At 0 Hit Points it is destroyed. When an enemy moves within 60 feet of it, you can use a Reaction to make it fire. Make a ranged attack roll using your Intelligence. On a hit the target takes 2d6 Radiant damage.",
 "Spectrum Visor": "A visor with one long slit full of blinking sensors. Choose one benefit below. It lasts until you take a Magic action to pick another. **Aurasight.** You sense magical effects within 30 feet. If you do, you can take the Magic action to see a faint aura around each visible creature or object there that carries magic, and you learn the school of magic of any effect made by a spell. 1 foot of stone, dirt, or wood, 1 inch of metal, or a thin sheet of lead blocks this sense. **Darkvision.** You gain Darkvision with a range of 60 feet, or if you already have it, its range grows by 60 feet. **Thermalsight.** You gain Thermalsight with a range of 60 feet, or if you already have it, its range grows by 60 feet.",
 "Stasis Generator": "Requires level 11. When you drop to 0 Hit Points, this Gadget triggers and wraps you in a shimmering, invulnerable sphere until the start of your next turn. Creatures, objects, and spells cannot pass through it. It weighs nothing and other creatures can pick it up and move it. While it lasts you cannot take damage or fail Death Saving Throws. At the start of your next turn, you regain Hit Points equal to your Gadgeteer level and the sphere vanishes. Once it triggers, it cannot do so again until you finish a Long Rest.",
 "Version 1812 Multirocket Launcher": "Requires level 11. As a Magic action, you unfold this multi-barrel rocket launcher and fire wildly into a 30-foot Emanation from you, playing a grand overture as you do. Each creature you choose in the Emanation makes a Dexterity save, taking 12d6 Fire damage on a failure or half on a success. Once you use it, you cannot do so again until you finish a Long Rest.",
}
