_AP = {
 "Experimental Frame": "You built a sophisticated exo-suit that boosts your strength and shields you. It counts as Heavy armor, you can don or doff it as a Bonus Action, you are trained with it, and no one else can wear it. While you wear it: **Size.** You become Medium if you are smaller. **Armor Class.** Your base AC is 10 plus your Dexterity and Intelligence modifiers, and you can still use a Shield with this benefit. **Temporary Hit Points.** At the start of each of your turns you gain Temporary Hit Points equal to your Gadgeteer level. Any left vanish when you doff the armor. **Life Suit.** The frame gives the benefits of a Life Suit. **Integrated Weapons.** You can build one Melee weapon into the frame, or two (one per arm) if neither has the 2H property. A drawn integrated weapon snaps to your hand and you cannot be disarmed of it. You can switch which weapons are integrated when you finish a Long Rest. When you attack with one, you can use your Intelligence modifier for the attack and damage rolls instead of Strength or Dexterity.",
 "M.A.C.": "You have a M.A.C., a Mechanized Autonomous Construct of your own design, driven by your AI companion. It uses the M.A.C. stat block and you decide how it looks, such as a cube on treads or an inflatable biped. **In Combat.** M.A.C. acts on your turn. It can move and use its Reaction on its own, but it only takes the Dodge action unless you spend a Bonus Action to command it to use an action from its stat block or another action. If you have the Incapacitated condition, M.A.C. acts on its own and is not limited to Dodge. **Repairs.** As a Utilize action you can temporarily repair M.A.C. at 0 Hit Points. It can move again but has the Incapacitated condition until it regains Hit Points or finishes a Long Rest. It gains the benefits of Short Rests and Long Rests as normal. If you lose it, you can build a new one for 250 CR. **Customizing.** M.A.C. has two integrated weapons in its arms. When you finish a Long Rest you can swap either for a new weapon without the 2H property. M.A.C. uses your Intelligence for attack and damage rolls with them.",
 "Utility Matrix": "You engineered a device that shifts shape and function quickly. You decide how it looks, such as a belt of tools or a rearranging cube. You can use the options below as a Bonus Action. After you use an option, you cannot use that same option again until the end of your next turn. **Blink Button.** Teleport up to 10 feet to an unoccupied space you can see. **Cloaking Device.** You have the Invisible condition until the end of the current turn. It ends early right after you make an attack roll, deal damage, or cast a spell. **Forcefield Projector.** Until the start of your next turn, you gain a bonus to AC equal to your Intelligence modifier. **Grappling Hook.** Pick a point you can see within 30 feet. You pull yourself to it in a straight Line.",
}
